--TEST--
Each operator PHP has and Novis does not — `and`, `or`, `xor`, `===`, `!==`, `<>`, `+` over two arrays, a subscript on a `string` and `++` on one — is reported at the operator itself and its help names the replacement, `rule:expressions/one-equality-operator`, `rule:types/arithmetic`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:expressions/operators-php-has-that-do-not-parse
// Every row of the chapter's table that is an operator proper. Each one is
// reported where it is written, with the help naming what to write instead,
// and the expectation below carries one diagnostic per row.
bool $p = true;
bool $q = false;
var $word = $p and $q;
var $either = $p or $q;
var $one = $p xor $q;
int $n = 1;
var $identical = $n === $n;
var $notIdentical = $n !== $n;
var $angled = $n <> $n;
array<int> $xs = [1];
array<int> $ys = [2];
var $joined = $xs + $ys;
string $s = "abc";
var $first = $s[0];
$s++;
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0226]: `and` is not supported
  --> %s:8:16
  |
8 | var $word = $p and $q;
  |                ^^^ Novis keeps exactly one spelling for each logical connective
  = help: use `&&` instead — it is the only logical connective Novis keeps

error[E0226]: `or` is not supported
  --> %s:9:18
  |
9 | var $either = $p or $q;
  |                  ^^ Novis keeps exactly one spelling for each logical connective
  = help: use `||` instead — it is the only logical connective Novis keeps

error[E0226]: `xor` is not supported
   --> %s:10:15
   |
10 | var $one = $p xor $q;
   |               ^^^ Novis keeps exactly one spelling for each logical connective
   = help: there is no direct replacement — write `(a || b) && !(a && b)`, or `a != b` when both operands are already `bool`

error[E0232]: `===` is not supported
   --> %s:12:21
   |
12 | var $identical = $n === $n;
   |                     ^^^ Novis keeps exactly one equality operator
   = help: use `==` — it never converts either operand, so there is nothing for `===` to distinguish

error[E0232]: `!==` is not supported
   --> %s:13:24
   |
13 | var $notIdentical = $n !== $n;
   |                        ^^^ Novis keeps exactly one equality operator
   = help: use `!=` — it never converts either operand, so there is nothing for `!==` to distinguish

error[E0241]: `<>` is not supported
   --> %s:14:18
   |
14 | var $angled = $n <> $n;
   |                  ^^ Novis spells inequality one way
   = help: use `!=` — it is the same comparison, and `<>` is the second spelling PHP inherited from its own predecessors

error[E0467]: `+` is not defined with an array operand
   --> %s:17:15
   |
17 | var $joined = $xs + $ys;
   |               ^^^^^^^^^ array operand of `+`
   = help: use `Core\Arr::underlay($a, $b)`, which keeps the left array's value at every key both of them have — the one operation `$a + $b` ever meant

error[E0482]: `string` cannot be subscripted
   --> %s:19:14
   |
19 | var $first = $s[0];
   |              ^^ this is `string`
   = help: `rule:types/string-is-utf8` indexes a `string` by extended grapheme cluster, which is said out loud rather than spelled with a subscript — `Core\Str::slice($s, $i, 1)`, or `Core\Bytes::slice` for a byte offset

error[E0474]: `++`/`--` has no meaning for `string`
   --> %s:20:1
   |
20 | $s++;
   | ^^^^ an increment is `± 1`, and this is not a number
   = help: `rule:types/arithmetic`'s arithmetic is over `int`, `uint`, `float` and `decimal`; PHP's string increment does not exist in Novis, because a binding never changes type

error: aborting due to 9 errors
